Cancer-cell-activatable image-guided photodynamic therapy with enhanced therapeutic effect is realized by constructing MOF-199-assisted nanoplatforms. MOF-199 restrains ROS generation of photosensitizers (PSs) in PS-loaded MOF-199 nanoparticles. After PS-loaded MOF-199 nanoparticles are endocytosed by cancer cells, MOF-199 greatly scavenges glutathione and collapses to release the PSs. Under light irradiation, cancer-cell-specific photosensitization is achieved to effectively kill cancer cells with minimum ROS loss from glutathione.
Keyword: activatable photodynamic therapy, photosensitizers, aggregation-induced emission, metal-organic frameworks, glutathione
